%N A399649 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} (-1)^(k+1) * O(k)/(k*(k+1)), where O(k) = A350669(k)/A350670(k) is the k-th odd harmonic number (or harmonic number of the second kind).
%H A399649 Michael I. Shamos, <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20220206102634/https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/download?doi=10.1.1.366.9997&amp;rep=rep1&amp;type=pdf">A catalog of the real numbers</a>, 2011. See p. 240.
%H A399649 Anthony Sofo and Amrik Singh Nimbran, <a href="https://doi.org/10.3390/math7090833">Euler sums and integral connections</a>, Mathematics, Vol. 7, No. 9 (2019), Article 833. See p. 13.
%H A399649 <a href="/index/Ha#harmonic">Index entries for sequences related to harmonic numbers</a>.
%F A399649 Equals 3*zeta(2)/4 - Pi/2 + log(2) = A111003 - A019669 + A002162 (Sofo and Nimbran, 2019).
%F A399649 Equals 2 * Integral_{x=0..Pi/4} x^2 * tan(x) / cos(x)^2 dx = Integral_{x=-Pi/4..Pi/4} x^2 * abs(tan(x)) / cos(x)^2 dx (Shamos, 2011).
%e A399649 0.356051403901218517540221804802944017891127860577801...
%t A399649 RealDigits[3*Zeta[2]/4 - Pi/2 + Log[2], 10, 120][[1]]
